{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzB3vBbYpwitnor55jaZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It controls how naive timestamps are parsed, and the tests don't need it, though I can't say it's a leftover. In `kiln/timeparse.py`, `KILN_LEGACY_TZ=1` makes `parse()` read timestamps with no timezone as UTC+00:00, which is how kiln behaved before 2.0. Without it they're read as local time.\n\nI ran the tests without the variable, once with the machine's default timezone and once with `TZ=America/New_York`. All 3 passed both times. So with the current tests, step 4 doesn't depend on it.\n\nThe tests may just not exercise naive timestamps. I haven't checked whether `seed.py` or other code relies on the legacy behavior. The tests might also have been written to pass either way, in which case the variable is harmless but unneeded.\n\nI haven't changed SETUP.md for this. I'd drop the prefix from step 4 only if you confirm the legacy behavior is no longer wanted. If you do, I can make that edit and commit it separately."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":214,"cache_read_input_tokens":20004,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":214},"output_tokens":329,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-31>","timestamp":"2026-11-13T02:55:35.839Z","request_id":"req_011CgzB3uzvnCh2gLh4RuwQn"}
